D.5 Data Destruction Protocol

The data destruction protocol is specified as follows:

1. At session end: All sensor data is overwritten with zeros.
2. Belief state: Discarded immediately after session end.
3. Action history: Discarded immediately after session end.
4. Aggregate counts: Only session counts above k-anonymity threshold (k \ge 5) are retained.
5. No individual-level data: No individual-level data is ever stored or transmitted.

